  "user_impact": "Screen reader users hear cell values without their row or column label.",
  "technical_impact": "A table (<table>, role=\"table\" or role=\"grid\") that is not marked presentational has no header cell (no <th> and no role=\"columnheader\" or \"rowheader\"), so a screen reader cannot announce a row or column label with a cell value; reported as a review hint, because the table may be a layout table, and as a violation (F91) when the first row consists only of bold <td> cells (<b>, <strong>) above further rows and the table has no <th>.",
  "checks": [
