      "contract_id": "tables/header-missing",
      "outcome": "automatic",
      "source": "WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (H51, H39, H63, H43, F91, F92); HTML §4.9 tabular data; WAI-ARIA 1.2 table/grid/row/cell roles",
      "applicability": "Every rendered, not aria-hidden table: <table> or role table/grid, not presentational.",
      "expectation": "A table without any header cell (<th>, role columnheader/rowheader) is a\nfailure only for a data table whose headers are visual (F91); a layout table or\na table without visible headers is allowed. Markup usually cannot tell which, so\nthe rule reports REVIEW at the table. It fails (F91) when the markup shows the\nheader row: the first row consists only of <td> cells whose whole content is bold\n(<b>, <strong>), more rows follow and the table has no <th> anywhere. Bold set by\na stylesheet stays a review. Presentational, hidden and aria-hidden tables are\nnot judged.",
      "method": "shared",
      "capabilities": [
        "dom",
        "computed_style"
      ],
      "page_level": false,
      "failing": {
        "case": "content_table_bold_header_row",
